Assignment 02: Binary Search and Recursive Analysis

Programming Task: Binary Search and Recursive Analysis
Implement binary search from scratch in C++17. Your program must work on a sorted vector and return the index of the target or -1 when the target is absent.

Required implementation
Implement an iterative binary search.
Implement a recursive binary search.
Instrument both versions to count element comparisons.
Test at least five searches, including: first element, last element, middle element, missing value below the range, and missing value inside the range.
For the recursive version, write and explain the recurrence T(n) = T(n/2) + O(1) and connect it to O(log n).
Compare binary search to a linear search on the same data.
Restriction: do not call std::binary_search, lower_bound, or another library search routine to perform the required search.

#Binary Search Assignment

## Description:
This program compares 3 search methods: Iterative Binary Search, Recursive Binary Search, and Linear Search using C++17. Each of the search methods looks for a target in the vector and returned the index
of the value, if found. If not, returned -1. 

##Approach:

Used a while loop for the iterative binary search with low, high and mid values. Used an if statement for the recursive binary search. For the linear search used a for loop that starts at the beginning of the vector
and will go through each element until target is found. If no target found at the end of the vector, returned -1. Used 5 test cases. 

